    // The bow light and the two running lights, at nine, twelve and six o'clock on FJ's top view, on the
    // flat of the saucer's outer ring.  They are built as the homing beacon is: a collar with a rounded
    // top edge, the plating's own, and on it a lamp, a low spherical cap.  FJ draws each as two circles,
    // the collar 0.101 and the lamp 0.053 in radius, centered 6.113 out; they are made half as large
    // again, 0.1515 and 0.0795, so that they still read at a distance, and the heights keep the
    // beacon's proportions.  Each keeps the gap FJ leaves between its collar and the rim, 0.0985, so
    // its center comes in to 6.0625.  The lamps glow as the beacon's does, in the colors such lights
    // always are: white at the bow, green to starboard and red to port.
    group {
        // the bow light
        lathe {
            path {
                move to 0, -0.0100
                line to 0.1515, -0.0100
                line to 0.1515, 0.0394
                curve 0.1515, 0.0612, 0.1338, 0.0788 to 0.1121, 0.0788
